const title = "Preservation of the Qur’an · 2.1 · IGCSE Islamiyat";
const footerHtml = "Cambridge IGCSE Islamiyat 0493 &middot; Paper 1, Topic 2, Unit 2.1";
const mainHtml = "<section class=\"chapter\">\r\n      <div class=\"wrap\">\r\n        <div class=\"chapter-head\">\r\n          <h1>Preservation of the Qur&rsquo;an</h1>\r\n          <p class=\"ch-sub\">2.1 The Revelation of the Qur&rsquo;an &middot; how the text was safeguarded during the Prophet's own lifetime</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p class=\"lede prose-col\">Even though receiving revelation could be physically overwhelming, the text itself was carefully safeguarded from the very start &mdash; well before it was ever gathered into a single book. This lesson is the bridge into Unit 2.2, which covers what happened after the Prophet's death.</p>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"steps\">\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">1</span>\r\n            <div><h4>Written down by literate companions</h4><p>The Prophet appointed scribes of revelation, who recorded each verse as it came &mdash; on whatever material was available: pieces of leather, flat stones, the shoulder-bones of camels, and palm-leaf stalks.</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">2</span>\r\n            <div><h4>Recorded in the order it arrived, not the order it was later arranged</h4><p>Because revelation came down in portions responding to specific situations across 23 years, verses were not written &mdash; or later arranged in the mus-haf &mdash; strictly in the order they were revealed.</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">3</span>\r\n            <div><h4>Checked annually with Jibreel</h4><p>Every Ramadan the Prophet recited the whole of the Qur&rsquo;an revealed so far to Jibreel, who reviewed it with him &mdash; a check on accuracy that happened twice in the final Ramadan of his life.</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">4</span>\r\n            <div><h4>Not yet a single book</h4><p>What did not exist yet was one bound volume gathering every verse together in a fixed order &mdash; that step only came after the Prophet's death, once revelation itself had ended (covered in full in Unit 2.2).</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"box box-source\">\r\n          <p class=\"box-label\">&#9633; Common mix-up to avoid</p>\r\n          <p>Don't confuse the Prophet's yearly review of the Qur&rsquo;an <em>with Jibreel</em> during his own lifetime with the later event where companions compared their <em>written copies</em> against each other. That second event &mdash; triggered by Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman's warning about regional recitation disputes &mdash; belongs to &rsquo;Uthman's standardisation in Unit 2.2, roughly two decades after the Prophet's death, not to the preservation process described here.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div style=\"max-width:66ch; margin:40px auto 0;\" class=\"prose-col\">\r\n          <h3 style=\"display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap;\">Ready to practise?</h3>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-top:10px; color:var(--ink-soft);\">A short Practice Quiz first, then a graded Quiz once you're confident. After that, take Unit 2.1's Unit Test.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"lesson-pager\">\r\n          <a class=\"pager-link\" href=\"../makki-madani-surahs/quiz.html\"><span class=\"pg-label\">&larr; Back</span><div class=\"pg-title\">Makki and Madani Surahs Quiz</div></a>\r\n          <a class=\"pager-link next\" href=\"practice.html\"><span class=\"pg-label\">Next &rarr;</span><div class=\"pg-title\">Practice Quiz</div></a>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>";
---

